---
import { blob } from "../consts";
import GitHubButton from "./GitHubButton.astro";
---

<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="wrap status">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Project status</p>
      <h2>Early, and built in public.</h2>
      <p>
        It runs real SEO work for its author, but expect rough edges, breaking changes in the data
        format (handled by numbered migrations) and only one model provider for now. The direction
        is in <a href={blob("docs/SLICES.md")}>SLICES.md</a>, and every non-obvious choice, with its
        reason, is in <a href={blob("docs/DECISIONS.md")}>DECISIONS.md</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="contrib">
      <h3>Contribute</h3>
      <p>
        From a typo to a new connector. Small pull requests, the Contract first, and no technical
        debt merged. Open an issue first for anything larger than a fix.
      </p>
      <p class="ctas">
        <GitHubButton label="Star or fork on GitHub" class="btn-primary" />
        <a class="btn" href={blob("CONTRIBUTING.md")}>Contributing guide</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
